<style>
  @page {
    size: A4;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .page {
    width: 794px;
    height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px;
    box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden;
    page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial, "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans";
  }
  .page:last-child {
    page-break-after: auto;
  }
  h1, h2, h3 {
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Helvetica", Arial;
  }
  .header-banner {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .logo {
    width: 100px;
    height: auto;
    margin-right: 20px;
  }
  .title {
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: bold;
    color: #333;
  }
  .image-container {
    width: 100%;
    height: 350px;
    margin-bottom: 30px;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .image-container img {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    object-fit: cover;
  }
  .section {
    margin-bottom: 30px;
  }
  .section-title {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #eee;
    padding-bottom: 5px;
  }
  .content-block {
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #333;
  }
  .signature-block {
    margin-top: 40px;
    padding-top: 20px;
    border-top: 1px solid #ccc;
  }
  .signature-block p {
    margin: 5px 0;
  }
  .divider {
    border-top: 1px solid #ccc;
    margin: 40px 0;
  }
  .callout-box {
    border: 1px solid #ddd;
    padding: 20px;
    margin: 20px 0;
    background-color: #f9f9f9;
  }
  .cta-button {
    display: inline-block;
    padding: 10px 20px;
    background-color: #0056b3;
    color: white !important;
    text-decoration: none;
    border-radius: 5px;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-top: 10px;
  }
  .footer-section {
    text-align: center;
    padding-top: 30px;
    border-top: 1px solid #eee;
    margin-top: 50px;
  }
  .social-icons a {
    margin: 0 10px;
    font-size: 24px;
    color: #555;
  }
  .passport-check-box {
    border: 2px solid #333;
    padding: 20px;
    margin: 20px auto;
    max-width: 500px;
    text-align: center;
  }
  .passport-check-box h3 {
    margin-top: 0;
  }
  .passport-list li {
    text-align: left;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .instagram-mockup {
    width: 100%;
    max-width: 400px;
    margin: 20px auto;
    border: 1px solid #ccc;
    padding: 10px;
    background-color: #fff;
  }
  .podcast-banner {
    text-align: center;
    margin: 40px 0;
  }
  .podcast-banner img {
    max-width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }
  .blog-section {
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 30px;
  }
  .blog-section h3 {
    margin-bottom: 15px;
  }
  .contact-footer {
    text-align: center;
    padding-top: 20px;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: #777;
  }
</style>

<div class="page">
  <div class="header-banner">
    <img src="" alt="Logo" class="logo">
    <div class="title">OFFICE OF GLOBAL EDUCATION</div>
  </div>

  <div class="image-container">
    <img src="" alt="Students group photo">
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Message from the Director</h2>
    <div class="content-block">
      <p>Hello and welcome back to Boston College!</p>
      <p>As we begin the fall {{ current_year }}, we at the Office of Global Education are excited to help begin preparing students for their opportunity to study abroad.</p>
      <p>If you are planning on studying abroad during the {{ start_year }}-{{ end_year }} academic year, planning for next year begins now. All students wanting to study abroad next academic year must apply by {{ application_deadline }}. This is the deadline for all semester study abroad applications (fall {{ current_year }}, fall {{ current_year + 1 }}, and spring {{ current_year + 1 }}). If you do not apply by {{ application_deadline }}, you cannot study abroad next academic year. Students may also opt to apply for a Summer {{ current_year + 1 }} faculty-led program or internship abroad by {{ summer_deadline }}. Learn more about OGE Summer Programs on our website.</p>
      <p>Students should carefully review our "Getting Started" page to learn how to begin. All students will need to complete an Initial Advising Questionnaire and attend a Study Abroad 101 to be eligible to apply to any semester study abroad program. This includes all Boston College and all approved, non-BC external programs. Our office offers multiple Study Abroad 101s each week until the end of the fall semester. Note that summer programs have different eligibility and application requirements and students can proceed to apply directly.</p>
      <p>Our website offers more details regarding programs abroad, requirements, academic considerations, financial questions, and other concerns. To complement our general advising and the website, OGE has several Program Managers (Study Abroad Advisors) who can answer your questions, address any concerns, and offer advice regarding abroad locations.</p>
      <p>Finally, after a three year hiatus, OGE is looking forward to having our first study abroad fair since {{ year_of_last_fair }}. More details regarding the fair can be found below.</p>
      <p>Regards,<br>
      <span data-field="director_name">{{ director_name }}</span><br>
      Director, Office of Global Education</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">We Are Open</h2>
    <div class="content-block">
      <p>We are excited to welcome new and returning students to a new year at Boston College. Our office is located in <span data-field="office_location">{{ office_location }}</span> across the street from McElroy Commons. We are open Monday through Friday 9:00am-5:00pm. This year we are happy to welcome the Office of Global Engagement and Office of International Students and Scholars to Hovey House as well. For assistance, call us at <span data-field="office_phone">{{ office_phone }}</span> or contact us at <span data-field="office_email">{{ office_email }}</span>.</p>
      <p>Study Abroad 101 information sessions will be held starting at the beginning of the semester. You can sign up for available sessions <a href="#" data-field="session_signup_link">{{ session_signup_link }}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section">
    <h2 class="section-title">Study Abroad Fair!</h2>
    <div class="content-block">
      <p>OGE supports students interested in going abroad on 200+ programs in 50+ countries! Please come out to the Study Abroad Fair to learn more about study, internship, service, and scholarship opportunities. The fair will take place <span data-field="fair_date">{{ fair_date }}</span> from <span data-field="fair_time">{{ fair_time }}</span> in the <span data-field="fair_location">{{ fair_location }}</span>. <a href="#" data-field="registration_link">{{ registration_link }}</a> to reserve a timed-entry slot for your visit. While no students will be turned away, this will help us plan better for your arrival, as we are expecting a large number of students to stop by. We look forward to seeing you soon!</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="divider"></div>

  <div class="page">
    <div class="section" style="text-align: center;">
      <h1 style="font-size: 60px; margin-bottom: 10px;">LET'S GO!</h1>
      <img src="" alt="Globe icon" style="width: 150px; margin-bottom: 20px;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 36px; margin-bottom: 10px;">STUDY ABROAD FAIR</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 18px;">CORCORAN COMMONS - <span data-field="fair_date_2">{{ fair_date_2 }}</span> - <span data-field="fair_time_2">{{ fair_time_2 }}</span></p>
      <div style="margin-top: 20px;">
        <img src="" alt="Instagram icon" style="width: 30px; height: 30px; vertical-align: middle; margin-right: 10px;">
        <span data-field="instagram_handle">{{ instagram_handle }}</span>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section" style="text-align: center;">
      <h2 class="section-title">IS YOUR PASSPORT UP-TO-DATE?</h2>
      <div class="passport-check-box">
        <h3>CHECK YOUR PASSPORT NOW!</h3>
        <ul class="passport-list">
          <li>Processing time for U.S. passports (new and renewals) is approximately <span data-field="us_passport_processing_time">{{ us_passport_processing_time }}</span>.</li>
          <li>In-person appointments (for first-time passports & lost/stolen passports) are extremely limited.</li>
          <li>Please note: many countries require that your passport be valid for <span data-field="passport_validity_period">{{ passport_validity_period }}</span> beyond your travel dates, and that you have at least one blank page.</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="margin-top: 20px;">SPRING ABROAD STUDENTS: HAVE YOU CHECKED THAT YOUR PASSPORT IS UP-TO-DATE?</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section" style="text-align: center;">
      <h2 class="section-title">Share Your Study Abroad Story</h2>
      <div class="content-block" style="text-align: center;">
        <p>This semester the Office of Global Education would like to give students to share their study abroad stories with the BC community and beyond. If you are planning to go abroad in Fall {{ current_year }}, Spring {{ current_year + 1 }}, or studied abroad in Summer or Spring {{ current_year + 1 }} and you are interested in sharing your story please <a href="#" data-field="story_submission_link">{{ story_submission_link }}</a>. You could be featured on our blog page, Instagram, or podcast.</p>
        <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
          <img src="" alt="Icon" style="width: 50px; height: 50px; margin: 0 15px;">
          <img src="" alt="Icon" style="width: 50px; height: 50px; margin: 0 15px;">
          <img src="" alt="Icon" style="width: 50px; height: 50px; margin: 0 15px;">
          <img src="" alt="Icon" style="width: 50px; height: 50px; margin: 0 15px;">
          <img src="" alt="Icon" style="width: 50px; height: 50px; margin: 0 15px;">
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section" style="text-align: center;">
      <p>Follow our IG account <span data-field="instagram_handle_2">{{ instagram_handle_2 }}</span> for the latest updates regarding the office and tons of student stories. Be sure to tag your photos with #bcabroad and #eaglesabroad for a shoutout.</p>
      <div class="instagram-mockup">
        <!-- Mock Instagram Feed -->
        <div style="text-align: center; font-size: 14px;">
          <img src="" alt="Instagram Header" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; padding: 10px;">
            <div style="font-weight: bold;">Boston College OGE</div>
            <div style="display: flex;">
              <span style="margin-right: 15px;">457 Posts</span>
              <span style="margin-right: 15px;">1,326 Followers</span>
              <span>234 Following</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-around; padding: 10px 0;">
            <img src="" alt="Icon" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;">
            <img src="" alt="Icon" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;">
            <img src="" alt="Icon" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;">
            <img src="" alt="Icon" style="width: 24px; height: 24px;">
          </div>
          <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 5px; padding: 10px;">
            <img src="" alt="Post 1" style="width: 100%; height: 100px; object-fit: cover;">
            <img src="" alt="Post 2" style="width: 100%; height: 100px; object-fit: cover;">
            <img src="" alt="Post 3" style="width: 100%; height: 100px; object-fit: cover;">
            <img src="" alt="Post 4" style="width: 100%; height: 100px; object-fit: cover;">
            <img src="" alt="Post 5" style="width: 100%; height: 100px; object-fit: cover;">
            <img src="" alt="Post 6" style="width: 100%; height: 100px; object-fit: cover;">
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section" style="text-align: center;">
      <a href="#" class="cta-button" data-field="podcast_link">{{ podcast_link }}</a>
    </div>

    <div class="section">
      <div class="content-block">
        <p>The Office of Global Education produces its very own podcast, Soaring to New Heights! This is a great way to hear about the experiences of BC students who are currently studying abroad or recently returned. Hear from students who have been to Spain, Austria, Ireland, and more! You can find the podcast on all major platforms. <a href="#" data-field="podcast_listen_link">{{ podcast_listen_link }}</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="podcast-banner">
      <img src="" alt="Soaring to New Heights Podcast Banner">
    </div>

    <div class="blog-section">
      <h3>Read Our Student Blogs</h3>
      <div class="content-block" style="max-width: 700px; margin: 0 auto;">
        <p><span data-field="student_name">{{ student_name }}</span> spent a summer in <span data-field="study_location">{{ study_location }}</span> completing the course Principles of Public Health: In the Happiest Place/ Public Health in a Global Society. Check out our OGE Blogs page to read more about her experience and other BC students abroad. <a href="#" data-field="blog_link">{{ blog_link }}</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="page">
    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 30px;">
      <img src="" alt="Copenhagen photo" style="width: 100%; height: auto;">
    </div>

    <div style="text-align: center; margin-bottom: 20px;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 28px; margin-bottom: 5px;">Office of Global Education</h2>
      <p style="font-size: 18px;">bc.edu/global-ed</p>
